    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d833">

                <pb facs="0917" n="825" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg825"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/11191</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-07T15:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 7, 1918, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1670. Department will be glad to have full report from you as soon as possible by
                    despatch on the present attitude of the Italian Government and of the various
                    Italian parties towards the territorial aspirations of the Jugo-Slavs.
                    Department considers this matter of great importance. See first paragraph your
                    1967, August 31, 11 a.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d833-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d833-f1" n="1" xml:id="d833-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed. The passage especially referred to read: “There appears to be a
                    growing feeling of distrust against Jugo-Slav National Committee and publication
                    of extracts unflattering to Italy from a book recently issued in Paris by above
                    committee has increased this.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
